WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
Three outline figures, nested like dolls.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.380
The outside one is a boy actor.

3
00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:09.660
Inside him is Viola, a young woman.

4
00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:14.000
Inside her is Cesario, the
young man she pretends to be.

5
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:17.760
On Shakespeare's public stage,
women didn't act at all.

6
00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.010
Not until 1660.

7
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:24.630
Then the countess Olivia reaches
out, towards the smallest figure.

8
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.560
A boy plays a girl playing a boy.

9
00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.930
So what does Shakespeare do with that?

10
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.590
In this mission, you'll peel
back each layer of the disguise,

11
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.530
and see who knows what.

12
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.640
You'll decode the riddles
Viola trades with Olivia.

13
00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:42.840
And you'll hear characters argue over
whether a woman's heart can hold as much

14
00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.520
love as a man's.

15
00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:48.530
Your mission: work out what
Shakespeare does with the layers.
